# CQ-26 · persona-identity
#
# Question: Which entities embody which Persona, in which document, and what
#           invariants does that Persona carry?
# Persona:  P3 — director / creative technologist. Character consistency across
#           shots is the problem a Persona exists for: the same identity, new
#           scene, new mood, same eyes.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.3.4 (`vso:Persona`, `vso:embodies`,
#           `vso:hasInvariant`); §3.1 (a Persona is a Frame, never depicted)
# Form:     SELECT — one row per persona invariant per embodying entity
# Note:     The query is written across documents — `?doc` is bound from the
#           graph the embodiment is asserted in — because that is what a Persona
#           is for: §5.3.4 says a Persona IRI MAY be shared by several VSON
#           documents, and this join is how a consumer would collect every scene
#           an identity appears in. **The shipped corpus exercises one.**
#           `12_persona` is the only document carrying a Persona, so every row
#           below names it. That proves the join and the invariant lookup run;
#           it does not show a Persona shared across documents, because no such
#           pair is shipped. The mechanism is checkable here, the multi-document
#           case is not, and this note is the difference.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?doc ?persona ?entity ?dimension ?value
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?entity  vso:embodies ?persona .
    ?persona a vso:Persona .
    OPTIONAL {
      ?persona   vso:hasInvariant ?invariant .
      ?invariant vso:dimension ?dimension ; vso:value ?value .
    }
  }
}
ORDER BY ?doc ?persona ?entity ?dimension
